# Declare a Data card

## Prerequisites

- py-wyrd installed and `WYRD_SERVER_URL` set
- A running server, pandas

## Recipe

```python
import pandas as pd
from wyrd.data import DataCard, PandasInterface

# 1. Infer the interface from a DataFrame
df = pd.DataFrame({
    "user_id": ["u1", "u2", "u3"],
    "churn_score": [0.12, 0.87, 0.45],
    "label": [0, 1, 0],
})
interface = PandasInterface.from_dataframe(df)

# 2. Build the card
card = DataCard(
    name="churn-scores-2024q4",
    version="0.1.0",
    spec=interface.to_spec(),
)

# 3. Optionally save locally
card.save()

# 4. Register
import wyrd
wyrd.cards.register(card)
```

## Notes

- `PandasInterface.from_dataframe` infers column types, row count, and basic
  statistics. You can override any field in the returned spec.
- `card.save()` writes `.wyrd/<space>/<name>/<version>/card.json` locally. This
  step is optional before registration.
- Registration is idempotent on identity; re-registering the same (name, version)
  with the same spec is a no-op.

